{
  "proposals": [],
  "assessments": [
    {
      "claim": "H3",
      "status": "reject",
      "investigation": "closed",
      "evidence": [
        "R3",
        "R13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "H17",
      "status": "accept",
      "investigation": "active",
      "evidence": [
        "R5"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "The new validation evidence for H3 changes the assessment of the EGFR claim. H3 was registered with direction -1, so a positive signed estimate corresponds to a raw exposed-minus-comparator difference below the comparator, meaning stronger EGFR dependency in EGFR-amplified cells. The discovery estimate for H3 was signed +0.025, which was near a roughly 10% relative effect scale but had a 95% interval that barely included zero. The independent validation estimate is signed only +0.006, with interval -0.034 to +0.045. Interpreted on the raw scale, validation therefore shows an EGFR-amplified minus non-amplified difference of about -0.006 EGFR dependency units, roughly 2% relative to the EGFR dependency mean, with uncertainty including null and clinically meaningful differences in both directions. The validation point estimate is far below the clinical-significance threshold and does not corroborate the borderline discovery result. Therefore the combined evidence does not support a reliable clinically meaningful association between EGFR amplification and stronger EGFR dependency in this dataset; H3 is rejected and closed.\n\nI also reassess the reversed KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 claim H17 using the same direct discovery evidence that caused the original H5 direction to be rejected. H17 is registered with direction +1, and its evidence is signed +0.796 with a very tight interval +0.776 to +0.816. On the raw scale, this means KEAP1-loss cells have higher, less-negative dependency_NFE2L2 scores, i.e. weaker NFE2L2 dependency than KEAP1-intact cells, by a magnitude far above a 10% relative effect scale. This association is very large and precisely estimated within this dataset, so I accept H17 as a dataset-specific association while explicitly reserving mechanistic or generalizability claims. The original H5 claim remains rejected because the observed direction is opposite to the pre-specified stronger-dependency direction.\n\nThe previously accepted H6, H7, and H11 remain supported associations in this dataset: SMARCA4 loss is associated with markedly stronger SMARCA2 dependency; MSI-high is associated with markedly stronger WRN dependency; and PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency. The technical POLR2A library control was not informative, and the next priority is specificity. If SMARCA4 loss, MSI-high, PTEN loss, or KEAP1 loss also produces large differences in the broadly essential POLR2A dependency score, that would suggest global screen or cell-state confounding and should lead to reassessment of these accepted associations. The most informative next analyses are therefore the reversed KEAP1-loss claim H17 already registered, the four POLR2A specificity controls H18-H21, and the still-untested direct pathway comparisons H13-H16. If the POLR2A controls are null, the accepted associations can remain strong dataset-specific findings; if any control is large, I will downgrade the corresponding accepted association as possibly non-specific. These conclusions are not causal and do not establish generalizability beyond the supplied dataset.",
  "research_notes": "Updated dataset-specific status after iteration 1: Accepted/rejected claims: H6 accept active, H7 accept active, H11 accept active, H17 accept active (KEAP1-loss associated with weaker/less negative NFE2L2 dependency). H3 now reject/closed after validation: discovery was borderline signed +0.025, validation signed +0.006 with interval crossing zero and point below 10% relative threshold; EGFR amplification not supported as a reliable strong-EGFR-dependency marker here. H5 reject/closed as originally registered because direction was opposite to the observed association; H2 and H10 remain rejected/closed. H12 remains an uninformative technical control, closed. H1, H4, H8, and H9 remain deferred/weak. Next analysis priorities: H17 direct reversed KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 confirmation and interpretation; H18-H21 POLR2A specificity controls for SMARCA4 loss, MSI-high, PTEN loss, and KEAP1 loss; H13-H16 untested direct comparisons for RIT1/KRAS, RPL11/TP53, KIF18A/MYC, and TMED10/EGFR. Do not yet interpret accepted associations as causal or generalizable; use POLR2A specificity controls and possibly independent validation later to decide whether they are robust dataset-specific associations or reflections of broader dependency/screen confounding."
}

{
  "proposals": [
    {
      "outcome": "dependency_SMARCA2",
      "exposure": "arid1a_loss",
      "direction": -1,
      "anticipated_direction": -1,
      "initial_status": "unresolved"
    },
    {
      "outcome": "dependency_STAT3",
      "exposure": "pik3ca_mutation",
      "direction": -1,
      "anticipated_direction": -1,
      "initial_status": "unresolved"
    },
    {
      "outcome": "dependency_USP7",
      "exposure": "tp53_loss",
      "direction": 1,
      "anticipated_direction": 1,
      "initial_status": "unresolved"
    },
    {
      "outcome": "dependency_EGFR",
      "exposure": "kras_mutation",
      "exposed": 0,
      "comparator": 1,
      "direction": -1,
      "anticipated_direction": -1,
      "initial_status": "unresolved"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "I am registering four targeted new comparisons to run alongside the eight already untested registered comparisons H13-H16 and H18-H21, so the next analysis batch can contain 12 informative tests. The accepted claims so far are SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency, PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency, and KEAP1 loss with weaker/less-negative NFE2L2 dependency. The four new claims are designed to test nearby biology and context effects rather than repeat existing comparisons. First, arid1a_loss versus intact is a new direct predictor for dependency_SMARCA2. ARID1A and SMARCA4 are SWI/SNF complex components, so loss of another BAF component could produce a similar synthetic-lethal-like dependency on SMARCA2; registered direction -1 expects a more negative dependency score in arid1a-loss cells. Second, pik3ca_mutation versus wild type is a direct test for dependency_STAT3. Activating PIK3CA mutations can increase PI3K/AKT/STAT3 signaling, and PTEN loss already showed a positive association with stronger STAT3 dependency, so I anticipate a more negative STAT3 dependency score in PIK3CA-mutant cells; direction -1. Third, tp53_loss versus intact is a direct test for dependency_USP7. USP7 participates in MDM2-p53 regulation, and cells with TP53 loss are plausibly less dependent on USP7 through that axis, which would appear as a higher/less-negative dependency score in TP53-loss cells; direction +1. Fourth, EGFR dependency in KRAS wild-type versus KRAS mutant cells tests molecular context after EGFR amplification alone failed validation. If KRAS mutant cells bypass EGFR, they may be less EGFR-dependent, producing a more negative raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast for KRAS wild type and thus a positive signed estimate under direction -1. Alternative outcomes are null or opposite associations, which would argue against these mechanistic predictions and would be treated as evidence that the associations are not general across measured molecular contexts in this dataset. These claims are dataset-specific associations only; causality, therapeutic implication, and generalizability remain outside the immediate evidence.",
  "research_notes": "Current dataset-specific status: accepted associations are H6 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency, H7 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency, H11 PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency, and H17 KEAP1 loss -> weaker/less-negative NFE2L2 dependency. H3 was rejected after validation; EGFR amplification does not appear reliable for stronger EGFR dependency. H5/H17 is direction-reversed KEAP1 association. Rejected direct controls include H2 BRAF/BRAF, H10 MYC/DHX9, and H3 EGFR/EGFR. H12 is a closed technical library control. Deferred weak direct comparisons remain H1 KRAS/KRAS, H4 ERBB2/ERBB2, H8 TP53/MDM2, and H9 MYC/USP7. Next analysis target: analyze the eight existing untested active comparisons H13-H16 and H18-H21, plus the four newly registered comparisons H22-H25, to total 12. This batch prioritizes (1) untested direct pathway links, (2) POLR2A specificity controls for accepted exposures, and (3) nearby biological refinements of accepted pathways. Do not yet interpret accepted associations as causal or generalizable. If POLR2A controls show large effects, reassess accepted effects as possible non-specific global/screen/cell-state associations. If controls are null, accepted effects remain credible dataset-specific associations, subject to later validation or subgroup follow-up."
}
